ezy-view (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Market data accuracy: symbol-metadata precision everywhere (no more
    hard-coded 2-decimal DOM), one shared trading day for loss/cooldown/journal,
    honest time-and-sales labeling, safe quote access and copied positions.
  * Persistence: journal and screenshots moved to IndexedDB with compression,
    a shared per-symbol quote poller (paused while hidden), and workspace
    export/import for layouts, drawings, alerts, watchlist and Pine scripts.
  * Packaging and runtime: MCP runtime status card + shipped ezyview-mcp
    wrapper, AppStream metainfo, extra icons, man pages, GitLab/Ubuntu package
    checks in CI, and MT5 bridge shipped with a token-generating launcher.
  * Security: Pine execution moved to a Web Worker with a hard time budget and
    factory-reset/shell-settings capabilities gated per command.
  * Performance: O(n·p) indicator loops replaced with single-pass streaming
    helpers (100k-bar benchmark script), Pine series-aware nz, per-bar var
    collapse, and a full-script compat suite.
  * Journal: pre-trade plans with plan-vs-execution R:R, review stats, bulk
    edit, import pipeline and account-aware filters.
  * Trading: trailing-stop and OCO order types in the paper engine with
    safety gates, plus order-flow/heatmap panels that degrade honestly on
    quote-only feeds.

 -- printezy247 <printezy247@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ezy-view (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Trading safety: closing or reducing a position no longer requires free
    margin, a rejected close is reported in the UI, and MetaTrader 5 stop/target
    amends target the position ticket without clearing the other level.
  * Debian policy compliance: maintainer contact, libc6 dependency, changelog,
    copyright, man page and AppStream metadata are now shipped.
  * Tag-triggered release workflow with lintian, package-content,
    desktop-file-validate, AppStream and install/launch smoke gates.
  * Version consistency is checked across all four version declarations.
  * Ship the MetaTrader 5 bridge with a launcher that generates a per-install
    token; the bridge now refuses trade writes when no token is configured.
  * Read the launcher's token automatically and document the Wine Python
    prerequisite instead of implying Wine alone is enough.

 -- printezy247 <printezy247@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

